  "worked_solution": "First, we express the given information in terms of $\u03a6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.90 \\\\ \u03a6(z) & =0.90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={\u03a6}^{-1}(0.90).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.90,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.90\\,\u21d2\\,{\u03a6}^{-1}(p)=1.2816.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={\u03a6}^{-1}(0.90)=1.2816.\n$$",
